modifying the repetition\ncount (to 6), modifying the turning angle (to 60), using join to turn\nthe result back into a ringed definition, and using the define block\nto create a new hexagon block.","position":{"start":{"line":63,"column":1},"end":{"line":63,"column":1}},"key":"qMMWb80mTD"}],"key":"qFbbS8htw1"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":75,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The define block has three “input” slots. The quotation marks are there\nbecause the first slot is an upvar, i.e., a way for define to provide\ninformation to its caller, rather than the other way around. In this\ncase, the value of block is the new block itself (the hexagon block, in\nthis example). The second slot is where you give the ","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"RF2n0GyuDY"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"label","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"SqnK1cxipN"}],"key":"EtSlWjL1k9"},{"type":"text","value":" for the new\nblock. In this example, the label is “hexagon _” in which the\nunderscore represents an input slot. So, here are a few examples of\n","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"UHxlfRgYOw"},{"type":"span","children":[{"type":"text","value":"block label","key":"gfefRtzUAu"}],"indexEntries":[{"entry":"block label","emphasis":false}],"label":"index-MACJdTaoIW","identifier":"index-macjdtaoiw","html_id":"index-macjdtaoiw","key":"qgqUYmpQgJ"},{"type":"text","value":" s:","position":{"start":{"line":68,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"key":"HXxTm0srYr"}],"key":"FRlMgK79VD"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"set pen _ to _","position":{"start":{"line":77,"column":1},"end":{"line":77,"column":1