.png","width":"1.22in","align":"center","key":"E4v3AfR087","urlSource":"images/11-metaprogramming/image376.png"},{"type":"text","value":"\nboth have the label","position":{"start":{"line":85,"column":1},"end":{"line":85,"column":1}},"key":"NyU6v1PuBu"}],"key":"A6zCf70XS8"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":96,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"_ of _. The label does not give the input slots names (that’s done in\nthe body, coming next) or types (that’s done in the set _ of block _\nto _ block, coming in two\nparagraphs).","position":{"start":{"line":93,"column":1},"end":{"line":93,"column":1}},"key":"chadutHnug"}],"key":"U3A3ZhcKxm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":101,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The third slot is for the ","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"key":"L6093sLIsk"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"definition","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"key":"IwedrpweyV"}],"key":"NiwKwHwieS"},{"type":"text","value":" of\nthe new block. This is a (ringed) script whose input names (formal\nparameters) will become the formal parameters of the new block. And the\nscript is its script.","position":{"start":{"line":98,"column":1},"end":{"line":98,"column":1}},"key":"T2ikMYfKi9"}],"key":"d4kFLCxQKK"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":107,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"So far we know the block’s label, parameters, and script. There are\nother things to specify about the block, and one purpose of the block\nupvar is to allow that. In the example on the previous page, there are\nfour set\n_ of block _ to _ blocks, reproduced below for your convenience:","position":{"start":{"line":103,"column":1},"end":{"line":103,"column":1}},"key":"z4gChC4Zwu"}],"key":"cmfiqzK2C4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":109,"column":1},"end":{"line":109,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/image951-ce1b078afafa2c57e0dcd59df8a951ea.png","alt":"image951.png","width":"2.83in","align":"center","key":"Cyaz1hj5Fr","urlSource":"images/11-metaprogramming/image951.png"}],"key":"lwOC6nT4zB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":120,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The category of the block can be set to any primitive or custom\ncategory. The default is other. The type is command, reporter, or\npredicate. Command is the default, so this setting is redundant, but we\nwant to show all the choices in the set block. The scope is either\nglobal or sprite, with global as the default. The last input to set\nslots is a list of length less than or equal to the number of\nunderscores in the label. Each item of the list is a type name, like the\nones in the is (5) a (number)? block. If there is only one input, you\ncan use just the name instead of putting it in a list. An empty or\nmissing list item means type Any.","position":{"start":{"line":111,"column":1},"end":{"line":111,"column":1}},"key":"S7SxWORLyk"}],"key":"CI1y73JjVJ"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":122,"column":1},"end":{"line":124,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It’s very important that these set blocks appear in the same script as the\ndefine that creates the block, because the block upvar is local to that\nscript. You can’t later say, for example,","position":{"start":{"line":122,"column":1},"end":{"line":122,"column":1}},"key":"XJrGzf96cL"}],"key":"mbCcvllFSB"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":126,"column":1},"end":{"line":126,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"image","url":"/build/image952-cda3b0577553565c05abeb71d5f0154f.png","alt":"image952.png","width":"4.31in","align":"center","key":"TZmeIvYBO4","urlSource":"images/11-m